\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)-9({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the cosine coefficients, we obtain \n\n$$\n-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)=\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$" 13194139535975 17592186045417 true] [17592186316630 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316403 13194139535975 17592186045417 false] [17592186316630 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315456 13194139535975 17592186045417 true] [17592186316630 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316403 13194139535975 17592186045417 false] [17592186316776 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316223 13194139535975 17592186045417 false] [17592186316776 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316129 13194139535975 17592186045417 true] [17592186316776 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316223 13194139535975 17592186045417 false] [17592186316832 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316280 13194139535975 17592186045417 false] [17592186316832 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316254 13194139535975 17592186045417 true]